"""hand-gesture-lab: record labelled hand-tracking sessions and replay them through the gesture engine (HQ-0221).

Usage:
  hand-gesture-lab record [--sections natural,grammar,everyday] [--quick] [--out DIR] [--no-window] [--then CMD]
  hand-gesture-lab replay REC_DIR [--engine PATH] [--config PATH] [--out PREFIX]
  hand-gesture-lab protocol

record   Guided prompts (large kitty window, sound cues) while the EagleEye Mini runs the same MediaPipe model as
         hand-gesture.service. Numbers only are kept: per hand the 21 landmarks in image and world coordinates, every
         canned gesture score, handedness, plus frame timing, inference time and mean luma. No image is stored.
         hand-gesture.service is stopped for the recording (the camera is exclusive) and restarted afterwards when it
         was running. Keys: Enter start a section, s skip a section, space pause (the current prompt restarts),
         x mark the current or previous prompt as botched, q stop and save.
         Output: ~/workspace/handgesture-review/data/rec-<stamp>/ {frames.jsonl.gz, labels.json, meta.json}.

replay   Feeds a recording through a GestureEngine (default: the installed hand-gesture next to this file; --engine
         takes a candidate) with a fake Hyprland world, at the daemon's frame cadence, in two passes:
         forced  - before each prompt the engine is put in the state the prompt assumes (armed, or idle for "arm";
                   a fullscreen window for "leave fullscreen"), so each gesture is scored on its own;
         natural - the engine runs uninterrupted from the first frame, as the daemon would.
         Writes <PREFIX>.md (tables) and <PREFIX>.json (every segment, event and log line); PREFIX defaults to
         REC_DIR/replay-<engine file name>.

Engine contract (what replay needs from a candidate): module attributes DEFAULT_MONITORS, CAPTURE_FPS, PROCESS_HZ,
ARMED_STATES, load_config(path); class GestureEngine(cfg, runner, wall_ms=, dispatch=, active=, windows=, monitors=,
pointer=) with update(now, frame, others), attributes state and mode; runner("down") = next workspace,
runner("up") = previous; Hyprland Lua dispatch strings for fullscreen and monitor moves; pointer.button(name, down)
for clicks. A module-level lab_force_arm(engine, now) / lab_force_idle(engine, now) overrides the built-in forcing.
"""
